text:
BAB II

ASAS DAN TUJUAN

Pasal 2

Asas Penyelenggaraan Perlindungan terhadap Korban Kekerasan Berbasis Gender dan Anak adalah: non diskriminasi;

kepentingan terbaik bagi korban;

keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;

perlindungan korban;

kelangsungan hidup dan tumbuh kembang anak;

penghargaan terhadap pendapat anak;

keterbukaan;

keterpaduan;

memberdayakan; dan kerahasiaan korban.

translated_text:
CHAPTER II

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

The Principles of Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children are: non-discrimination;

best interests of victims;

justice and gender equality;

victim protection;

survival and development of children;

respect for children's opinions;

openness;

integration;

empowering; and victim confidentiality.

text:
Pasal 3

Tujuan Penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Korban Berbasis Gender dan Anak adalah untuk: mencegah segala bentuk kekerasan berbasis gender dan kekerasan terhadap anak, yang terjadi di lingkup rumah tangga dan/atau masyarakat;

memberikan perlindungan berupa layanan pengaduan, layanan kesehatan, layanan rehabilitasi sosial, layanan bantuan dan penegakan hukum, serta layanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial; dan mengupayakan peningkatan partisipasi masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 3

The Objectives of Implementation of Protection for Gender-Based Victims and Children are to: prevent all forms of gender-based violence and violence against children, occurring within the scope of the household and/or community;

provide protection in the form of complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal assistance and enforcement services, and repatriation and social reintegration services; and seek to increase community participation.

text:
BAB III

BENTUK KEKERASAN

Pasal 4

Bentuk-bentuk kekerasan yaitu: kekerasan fisik;

kekerasan psikis;

kekerasan seksual;

penelantaran; dan/atau kekerasan lainnya.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III

FORMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 4

Forms of violence are: physical violence;

psychological violence;

sexual violence;

neglect; and/or other violence.

text:
UPPTK.

